 mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 120%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #000000; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="h3_text" data-groupid="h3" class="mobile_match"><span style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 120%;"><strong><a style="color: #000000; font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: none;" href="https://email.mckinsey.com/industries/industrials/our-insights/turning-humanoid-supply-chain-constraints-into-billion-dollar-wins?__hScId__=v710000019e67efa8bfbc29776e96c65848&__hRlId__=e8bc20255de04fe70000021ef3a0bcd4&__hDId__=e8bc2025-5de0-4fe7-9268-aeba118617bd&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-nsl-omcknsl-mgp-glb--&hlkid=3bae080911d34042bda392ce61b5e763&hctky=17208988&hdpid=e8bc2025-5de0-4fe7-9268-aeba118617bd#/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-link-id="a845be308db611ec92e885c76187d3bd"><span style="line-height: 120%;"><span style="font-family: Georgia, Times, serif; line-height: 120%;">Autonomy at scale</span></span></a></strong></span></h3> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-006: Headline | H3 --> </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-008: Paragraph | P1 --><section id="1008_p1" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p1_text" data-groupid="p1" class="mobile_match"><span style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 150%;"><strong>In the news.</strong> Autonomous robots are moving beyond pilots and into real-world operations. The World Economic Forum notes that robots can now work continuously in industrial spaces such as ports and warehouses, including moving shipping containers without human intervention. Still, experts say that full autonomy is years away: Costs remain high, standards vary, and robots perform best in tightly controlled settings. The next frontier for robotic intelligence is adapting to unpredictable environments and manipulating objects safely, which one executive says will require better hardware and improved risk assessment. <span style="color: rgb(5, 28, 44); text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%;">[</span><a style="color: #333333; text-decoration: none; font-weight: inherit;" href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019e67efa8bfbc29776e96c65848/e8bc20255de04fe70000021ef3a0bcd5/e8bc2025-5de0-4fe7-9268-aeba118617bd?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQFx9iUafXWFZ5Zwk7O1zEoS3QZdrhEVJIskb8PtCKsAxkxwNSfo_FHEaUc3ElMc2nhC6CKrfKmqKYOTuSiYhvxD6Nh7qCug2jKeWx5OFf377iK62egPLDnLLEQruT9uVUS9JSi-TU-pnspmk7JDTpUKnnA4huSfLpPz408wrnxQwZBHnHFLFxlev-mfYWg-mOW4PVOinOWBKJnBsry8pKXt-DTTjWP5rrr9zxW_rjrH1qfKtXZTW5pNhirDAAZ160c5-gtd0e9S3wKoMRR2vyER6l2Y3UsMwVvRykPbBQA28PnZeG-XdUM6O0EjVdOHyuNuTotNYN4v59TSzbJWpSQaQw2DSGigLsin5gaMQriCWnwjF2JaNBfYZ8FOIMYZHF2vL6dcRGdoWNLmY3-oZFj65ePjCavJV8T1C7FwPhuaH6mLiGfggy6GEsuHaajpx5-pRC5sLQvv_KJ-bZ5ghMw_KDAh2BWadtk_A5tX2iZcyeEoHzWcWNRvpPFANV5X84o3gTFPteb5_t" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-link-id="f260e8519d7f11f0b0e1ad3756d0fe1d"><span style="color: #2251ff; text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%;">WEF</span></a><span style="color: rgb(5, 28, 44); text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%;">] </span></span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></tab